{"shortDescription":"As we draw close to the end of the year, several large cap stocks continue to earn top marks from Seeking Alpha’s Quant system.The rankings point to strength across several sectors, although energy, financials, and technology-related stocks account for a significant share of the list. As of Nov. 27…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["As we draw close to the end of the year, several large cap stocks continue to earn top marks from Seeking Alpha’s Quant system."]},{"type":"p","children":["The rankings point to strength across several sectors, although energy, financials, and technology-related stocks account for a significant share of the list. As of Nov. 27, the top 112 ranked stocks carry a Strong Buy Quant Rating, with scores ranging from 4.50 to 4.99."]},{"type":"p","children":["Seeking Alpha’s Quant Ratings system grades stocks on their relative performance on key quantitative metrics. It hones in on stocks with the strongest combination of value, growth, profitability, EPS revisions, and price momentum relative to their sector peers."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Energy stocks lead the rankings"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Energy is the most prominent sector in the screen. Integrated oil and gas companies, refiners and exploration and production firms together account for a substantial number of the top-rated stocks."]},{"type":"p","children":["Marathon Petroleum ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:MPC","text":"NYSE:MPC"}}," ranks fourth overall with a 4.98 Quant score, followed by Valero Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:VLO","text":"NYSE:VLO"}}," at 4.98 and Phillips 66 ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PSX","text":"NYSE:PSX"}}," at 4.97. Chevron ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CVX","text":"NYSE:CVX"}},", Shell ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:SHEL","text":"NYSE:SHEL"}},", HF Sinclair ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:DINO","text":"NYSE:DINO"}},", ConocoPhillips ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:COP","text":"NYSE:COP"}},", TotalEnergies ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:TTE","text":"NYSE:TTE"}},", Repsol ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:REPYY","text":"OTC:REPYY"}},", Eni ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:E","text":"NYSE:E"}},", and Suncor Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:SU","text":"NYSE:SU"}}," also feature among the top 30."]},{"type":"p","children":["The broader list includes other energy names such as EOG Resources ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:EOG","text":"NYSE:EOG"}},", Permian Resources ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PR","text":"NYSE:PR"}},", Venture Global ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:VG","text":"NYSE:VG"}},", Cenovus Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CVE","text":"NYSE:CVE"}},", Canadian Natural Resources ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CNQ","text":"NYSE:CNQ"}},", and Diamondback Energy ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:FANG","text":"NASDAQ:FANG"}},"."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Semiconductors and technology hardware remain strong"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Semiconductors and technology hardware are another major cluster. Micron Technology ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:MU","text":"NASDAQ:MU"}}," is ranked second overall with a 4.99 Quant score, while Dell Technologies ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:DELL","text":"NYSE:DELL"}}," ranks third at 4.98."]},{"type":"p","children":["Advanced Micro Devices ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMD","text":"NASDAQ:AMD"}},", Texas Instruments ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:TXN","text":"NASDAQ:TXN"}},", and Sandisk ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SNDK","text":"NASDAQ:SNDK"}}," also make the top 30. Further down the ranking, ASE Technology ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:ASX","text":"NYSE:A